-- title:
--   Pointwise variation of the natural theta weight
-- statement:
--   Let $2\le a\le b\le X$ be natural numbers, $a\le m<b$, and $\log X/\log a\le5$. Put $q_m=\lfloor X/m\rfloor$, $u_m=\log q_m/\log m$, and $J_m=I(q_m,m)$, where $I$ is the base-free fractional correction. Let $\Theta_X(m)$ be the natural Saias main term at $(q_m,m)$ divided by $\log m$, and let $S_X(m)=q_m/\log m-q_{m+1}/\log(m+1)$ be the selector cell ledger.
--
--   With $\rho$ the Dickman function,
--   $$|\Theta_X(m+1)-\Theta_X(m)|\le16S_X(m)+\frac{X}{m\log m}\left(|\rho(u_{m+1})-\rho(u_m)|+|J_{m+1}-J_m|\right).$$
--
--   This separates coefficient drift from the two globally summable smooth variations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/RoughSaiasSharpCorrectionTarget.lean#L1208-L1326

